{{!-- Sidebar tab navigation — rendered inside the wh40k-sidebar container.
     Single vertical column of full-width buttons (#320): the nav stacks in one
     column on every sheet width rather than reflowing into two columns when wide.
     Styling applies to PC and NPC sheets.

     `tw-bg-transparent` is deliberately NOT important, unlike its neighbours. It
     has one job — beat stories/css/foundry-chrome.css's `.tabs` (0,1,0) in the
     Storybook cascade, where the sheet root is `div.wh40k-rpg.sheet` with no
     `.actor` and tailwind/legacy-components.js's nav rule therefore never matches.
     At (0,2,0) it does that and still loses, correctly, to that rule's (0,4,1)
     `background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.2)` inside Foundry. Carrying the important
     modifier it won BOTH, which is why that rule needed a priority flag to keep
     the tint (and why the modifier must not come back);
     deleting the utility outright is the other wrong answer — it strips the
     Storybook nav back to the chrome's elevated grey (8 screenshots). --}}
{{> systems/wh40k-rpg/templates/actor/partial/tab-strip.hbs
    tabs=tabs
    navClass="!tw-flex !tw-flex-col !tw-gap-1 !tw-m-0 !tw-p-2 !tw-w-full !tw-shrink-0 !tw-grow-0 tw-bg-transparent"
    itemClass="wh40k-nav-item tw-flex tw-w-full tw-items-center tw-justify-center tw-text-center tw-whitespace-nowrap tw-overflow-hidden tw-text-ellipsis tw-rounded-md tw-px-2 tw-py-1.5 tw-text-xs tw-border-b-2 tw-border-b-gold bc:tw-border-b-crimson-light dh1:tw-border-b-gold-raw-l5 dh2:tw-border-b-gold-raw dw:tw-border-b-accent-combat ow:tw-border-b-brass-l20 rt:tw-border-b-gold im:tw-border-b-failure tw-border-b-transparent"}}
